    "title": {
     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Two bells ring every 6 and 8 minutes. They ring together now.\n\"When will they ring together again?\" asked Ravi."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "HCF",
     "LCM",
     "multiple"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "The HCF (highest common factor) is the largest number that divides two numbers. The LCM (least common multiple) is the smallest number that both divide.\nFor 6 and 8, the multiples are 6, 12, 18, 24 and 8, 16, 24 so the LCM is 24. The bells ring together again after 24 minutes.\nUse HCF for sharing into equal groups and LCM for events repeating together."
    }
   },
